<title>SPAIN: Palma de Mallorca cargo traffic dips in September.</title>
<headline>Palma de Mallorca cargo traffic dips in September.</headline>
<dateline>PALMA DE MALLORCA, Spain 1996-10-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cargo traffic at Spain's Palma de Mallorca airport, the main gateway to the Balearic Islands, slipped to 1,945 tonnes in September from 1,960 in August and 2,032 in July.</p>
<p>Nearly 78 percent of the total was national traffic, 19 percent intra-European Union business and three percent was other international freight.</p>
<p>The accumulated total so far this year now stands at 14,487 tonnes.</p>
<p>The airport also handled 124 tonnes of mail in the month and two million passengers.</p>
<p>-- Air Cargo Newsroom Tel+44 171 542 7706 Fax+44 171 542 5017</p>
